sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Saadaoui et al. (2020), Serra et al. (2023) & Rozbicki et al. (2015) avian gastrulation tensile ring, Polonaise twin-vortex flow & primitive streak attractor — MorphoEval overall 67.3/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 re-score of `2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py` (67.3/100, down from 92.6 in Pass 2). Both Pass 2 remediation items were closed in code: an explicit Wnt8c -> Nodal -> FGF8 reaction-diffusion cascade with implicit spectral diffusion-decay and semi-Lagrangian advection now sources ring myosin through a pMLC activation field (`step_ligand_fields`, `myosin_phosphorylation_field`), with decay lengths verified against $\\lambda = \\sqrt{D/k}$ (FGF8 0.8 %, Nodal 1.4 %), and a reduced 2.5D apical-basal column model (`step_apical_basal_column`: apical constriction, basal expansion, constant-volume thickening $h = 2h_0/(a+b)$, basement-membrane decay, ingression rate $I$) feeds an irrotational sink $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf{v} = -I$ into the planar flow (`solve_ingression_sink_velocity`). Perturbations are now receptor-level: SU5402 gives a uniform ring (asymmetry 0.00), SB431542 and Y-27632 give zero ingression, ectopic Vg1 gives a bipolar ring, and the emergent 5-regime peak speeds rank-correlate with Saadaoui/Serra at $\\rho = 0.90$ under one WT-fixed calibration constant. Five Lean 4 theorems compile with 0 sorrys. The remediation, however, exposed that the v2 headline numbers (AP/ML 4.25, 2.40 um/min, $r = 1.0000$, SU5402 1.00) are prescribed lookups of the regime parameters, that about 82 % of the Polonaise flow is a hand-written streamfunction rather than the Stokes solution, and that the honest field-derived EMT zone is a posterior crescent (WT AP/ML 0.59 vs 4.25; 5-regime aspect $\\rho = -0.20$) because mediolateral intercalation is absent. The code now discloses all of this (NOTE flags, `measured_*` keys, Panel I), which is credited; the scores reflect what the coupled model actually produces. Overall 67.3/100 (faithfulness 64.0, reproducibility 75.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 68, Morphological realism / specimen match 58, Parameter expressivity 74, Morphometric validation 62, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 74, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: docs/media/gastrulation_streak_attractor_comparison.png: rendered output of 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py at 028758bc, image/png, 1754542 B, 2700×2400 px, artifact_sha256 74525e85617b6b2617c2da95d44896606c255ec050d0b3628822429a2641d5b2 (sha256 74525e85617b6b2617c2da95d44896606c255ec050d0b3628822429a2641d5b2), spec_fingerprint 394d38439dd8f3b351ba32f3eef22da12f99bfa222be7659901a95855eb8a1e1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 394d38439dd8f3b351ba32f3eef22da12f99bfa222be7659901a95855eb8a1e1; artifact_sha256: 74525e85617b6b2617c2da95d44896606c255ec050d0b3628822429a2641d5b2. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-gastrulation-streak-attractor-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Saadaoui, Rocancourt, Roussel, Corson & Gros (2020) Science 367:453-458 viscous epiblast Stokes model eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) = -nabla.(m Q) showing that a posterior-graded marginal Myosin-II tensile ring m(theta) = m_0 + delta_m cos(theta) and apical mesendoderm ingression drive counter-rotating Polonaise twin vortices and midline primitive streak elongation | Serra et al. (2023) mechanochemical active nematic feedback (Dm/Dt and DQ_{ij}/Dt) and Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) Dynamic Morphogenetic Skeleton demonstrating transition from a wild-type linear streak to a circular ring under FGF receptor inhibition (SU5402) or twin streaks under ectopic Vg1/Wnt induction | Yu et al. (2009) Fgf8 source-sink gradient with D = 53 um^2/s; Muller et al. (2012) Nodal D = 3.2 um^2/s, t1/2 = 95 min; Nakaya et al. (2008) streak-restricted basement-membrane breakdown during EMT; Voiculescu et al. (2014) SB431542 Nodal/ALK block abolishes ingression; reconstructed_in_script: 64x64 coupled 2D spectral viscous epiblast Stokes solver (Green's function L2 error = 5.97e-16) whose solution enters the planar flow with weight STOKES_ACTIVE_WEIGHT = 0.18 on top of a prescribed dipole + quadrupole Polonaise streamfunction and isotropic ring contraction, plus an irrotational sink driven by the EMT column ingression rate; active nematic Myosin-II cable advection-alignment PDE; Cauchy-Green FTLE ridge integration; semi-Lagrangian transport in physical units | Explicit Wnt8c (posterior marginal source) -> committed streak-cell density -> Nodal (autoactivating) -> FGF8 reaction-diffusion cascade with implicit spectral diffusion-decay and Hill-type pMLC activation P = rho_ROCK H(a_ALK N)(0.35 + 0.65 H(a_FGFR F)) sourcing ring myosin; decay lengths verified against sqrt(D/k) (FGF8 0.8 %, Nodal 1.4 %); receptor-level SU5402 (a_FGFR = 0), SB431542 (a_ALK = 0), Y-27632 (rho_ROCK), ectopic Vg1/Wnt (anterior source) regimes | Reduced 2.5D apical-basal column per grid point: apical area a (ROCK/pMLC-driven constriction), basal area b = 1 + chi_b (1 - a) B, constant-volume height h = 2 h0/(a + b), wedging index (b - a)/(b + a), basement-membrane integrity B decaying under Nodal/FGF gating, ingression rate I = k_ing Wdg (1 - B) feeding the planar sink (nabla.v = -I); field-derived readouts: streak thickening 1.26x, BM-broken area fraction 0.17, ingressed fraction 0.20, EMT-zone AP/ML 0.59, emergent ring asymmetry 0.63, peak speed 2.14 um/min (WT) | 15x15 (delta_m x beta_m) morphospace from 225 coupled 40x40 simulations; automated CV segmentation of HH1 Koller's sickle, HH2 condensation, HH3+ streak, area pellucida/opaca ratio (0.6250) and PIV bilateral symmetry (0.9705) on chick_primitive_streak_specimen.jpg; transfer_boundary: 2D planar circular epiblast continuum sheet of radius R = 1.15 mm with a single global velocity calibration constant U_CAL_MM_PER_H = 0.061 fixed on the wild-type regime (so the WT peak speed is calibrated, the other four regimes' speeds are emergent: Spearman rho = 0.90, Pearson r = 0.927 vs the Saadaoui/Serra table) | The coupled model forms a thickened, ingressing posterior crescent and does NOT elongate it into a midline streak within 8 h (WT EMT-zone AP/ML 0.59 vs reference 4.25; 5-regime aspect Spearman rho = -0.20): mediolateral intercalation (Rozbicki 2015) is absent and the active-nematic Stokes contribution is down-weighted to 0.18 to keep speeds physical | The four Pass 2 readouts streak_ap_ml_aspect_ratio / streak_length_mm / peak_polonaise_speed_um_min / ftle_ridge_anisotropy are retained as prescribed piecewise-analytic lookups of the regime parameters and reproduce the reference table by construction (r = 1); they are flagged in the code and are NOT evidence of model performance | Ligand kinetics for Wnt8c (D, half-life), FGF8 half-life, the column parameters (k_con, m_c, k_rel, chi_b, k_bm, k_ing, a_min, h0 = 25 um), source amplitudes and Hill constants are ASSUMED or DERIVED (marked as such in ligand_emt_reference.json); reference values 1.33 (thickening) and 0.08 (BM-broken fraction) are derived, not measured; does_not_claim: 3D finite-element epithelial mechanics, out-of-plane bending, bottle-cell mechanics or individual mesenchymal migration after ingression (the column model is a per-point 2.5D reduction) | Mediolateral cell intercalation or any mechanism that converts the posterior crescent into a 4:1 midline streak | Independent verification of the Serra et al. (2023) venue/DOI or of the four new ligand/EMT DOIs (all recorded as unverified offline)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:1064-1067, 1117-1120, 1406 and 1547-1558 — print the measured bounding boxes and ratios in Panel E instead of the hard-coded '61x183 px' / '135x81 px' / '5.00x', segment r_AO instead of fixing r_ao_px = 128, fix the docstring's 0.6406, and replace the self-referential PIV symmetry reference 0.9705 with a published bilateral-symmetry value or drop the measurement.",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:11-14, datasets/gastrulation_streak_attractor/paper_citations.bib:12-21, gastrulation_streak_attractor_reference.json and README.md — verify and correct the Serra et al. (2023) venue/DOI ('Nature Methods / Science Advances 20:1739-1748, 10.1038/s41592-023-02009-y' is inconsistent; likely Science Advances 9(49):eadh8152, 10.1126/sciadv.adh8152) and the four new DOIs (yu2009, muller2012, nakaya2008, voiculescu2014) against the publishers.",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:114-125 and datasets/gastrulation_streak_attractor/ligand_emt_reference.json:53-61,117-130 — source or replace the ASSUMED constants (Wnt8c D and half-life, FGF8 half-life, h0 = 25 um, k_con, m_c, k_rel, chi_b, k_bm, k_ing, a_min, s_W/s_N/s_F, k_ind, c_max, Hill K's) and the DERIVED reference values 1.33 and 0.08 with measured chick values (e.g. Rozbicki 2015 cell-shape data, Nakaya 2008 laminin breakdown extent); reconcile ALPHA_M_HR = 0.10 with the vendored alpha_m = 0.45 (update the JSON or the code, with a stated reason).",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:1727-1731, 105-107 and 1837-1851 — update the run_self_test docstring ('Pass 2 ... 3 Lean 4 theorem invariants' -> 5 theorems), remove or render OUTPUT_LIGAND_PNG, and add --out / --gif / --no-morphospace / --regime CLI flags so individual regimes and the 225-simulation morphospace can be run selectively; track the comparison PNG (gitignore exception) or render to a tracked path.",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:359-407 — replace the per-substep soft_wall clipping of the diffusible ligands with a proper absorbing / no-flux boundary at the disc edge and refine the grid (or subcycle the Wnt8c field) so that the 72 um Wnt8c decay length is resolved by more than two cells.",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:649-667 and 119 — the planar flow is a prescribed dipole + quadrupole streamfunction plus isotropic ring contraction with the Stokes solution down-weighted to STOKES_ACTIVE_WEIGHT = 0.18; solve the flow from the active stress alone (weight 1) with a viscosity/friction chosen so the WT speed is physical, and retire psi_dip / psi_quad / iso_ring_v* (Theorem 1 should then be stated about the solved field).",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:775-785 and 468-505 — the coupled model forms a posterior crescent (WT EMT-zone AP/ML 0.59 vs 4.25; 5-regime aspect Spearman rho = -0.20) because mediolateral intercalation (Rozbicki 2015) is absent; add a planar convergent-extension term (anisotropic active stress along the nematic director or an intercalation flux in the committed-cell density) and show the EMT zone elongating to AP/ML > 2 within 8 h at speeds < 3 um/min.",
            "remediation needed: 2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py:812-843, 1296-1366 and 972-981 — remove (or stop exporting as measurements) the prescribed piecewise-analytic lookups streak_ap_ml_aspect_ratio / streak_length_mm / peak_polonaise_speed_um_min / ftle_ridge_anisotropy and the circular pearson_r_aspect / pearson_r_speed; make the four retained Pass 2 measurements and Panel C read the field-derived `measured_*` values so that the measurement set can fail." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.673"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary, Pass 3 Phase B assessor) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

